                                                                     \n     Purpose: Cross-framework agent interoperability standard                                                                                                                        \n     - REST-based, supports all modalities (text, image, audio, video, binary)                                                                                                       \n     - Sync/async, streaming, stateful/stateless, online/offline discovery                                                                                                           \n     - Open standard under Linux Foundation (recently merged with A2A governance)                                                                                                    \n     - Key features: No SDK required (works with curl/Postman), MIME-type extensibility, async-first with sync support                                                               \n     - Use cases: Flexible agent replacement, multi-agent collaboration, cross-platform integration, inter-company partnerships                                                      \n     - Reference implementation: BeeAI platform                                                                                                                                      \n                                                                                                                                                                                     \n     SBP (Stigmergic Blackboard Protocol)                                                                                                                                            \n     Purpose: Decentralized multi-agent coordination via environment-based signals                                                                                                   \n     - Inspired by ant colony stigmergy — agents leave \"digital pheromones\" on a shared blackboard                                                                                   \n     - No centralized orchestrator needed, no direct agent-to-agent messaging                                                                                                        \n     - Key mechanics: Signal intensity, decay curves, decoupled awareness                                                                                                            \n     - Complements MCP — MCP answers \"what tools can I use?\" while SBP answers \"what's the state of the collective task?\"                                                            \n     - Production-ready for non-linear workflows, scalable and fault-tolerant                                                                                                        \n     - SDKs: TypeScript, Python; pluggable storage (in-memory, Redis, SQLite)                                                                                                        \n                                                                                                                                                                                     \n     MCP (Model Context Protocol)                                                                                                                                                    \n     Purpose: Standardizing how applications deliver tools, datasets, and sampling to LLMs                                                                                           \n     - Created by Anthropic, widely adopted                                                                                                                                          \n     - Client-server architecture (JSON-RPC 2.0)                                                                                                                                     \n     - Focus: LLM ↔ external tools integration                                                                                                                                       \n     - Strengths: Simple, well-documented, growing community                                                                                                                         \n     - Gaps: Lacks streaming, memory, async execution (addressed by ACP/A2A)                                                                                                         \n                                                                                                                                                                                     \n     A2A (Agent-to-Agent Protocol)                                                                                                                                                   \n     Purpose: Peer-to-peer agent collaboration                                                                                                                                       \n     - Originally Google, now under Linux Foundation with ACP                                                                                                                        \n     - Architecture: P2P using Agent Cards (HTTP)                                                                                                                                    \n     - Focus: Enterprise task delegation and inter-agent negotiation                                                                                                                 \n     - Message format: Task + Artifact (JSON)                                                                                                                                        \n     - Identity: DID-based handshake                                                                                                                                                 \n                                                                                                                                                                                     \n     ANP (Agent Network Protocol)                                                                                                                                                    \n     Purpose: Decentralized agent discovery and collaboration                                                                                                                        \n     - Architecture: Decentralized P2P using DIDs (Decentralized Identifiers)                                                                                                        \n     - Discovery: Search engine or .well-known/ endpoints                                                                                                                            \n     - Use case: Open-internet agent marketplaces                                                                                                                                    \n     - Strengths: Trustless identity, AI-native negotiation                                                                                                                          \n                                                                                                                                                                                     \n     Comparison Summary                                                                                                                                                              \n                                                                                                                                                                                     \n     | Aspect | MCP | ACP | A2A | SBP | ANP |                                                                                                                                        \n     |--------|-----|-----|-----|-----|-----|                                                                                                                                        \n     | Architecture | Client-Server | Brokered Client-Server | P2P | Blackboard | Decentralized P2P |                                                                                \n     | Discovery | Manual/Static | Registry-based | Agent Card | Shared Blackboard | Search Engine/DIDs |                                                                            \n     | Transport | HTTP, Stdio, SSE | HTTP + Streams | HTTP + SSE | Pluggable (Redis, etc.) | HTTPS |                                                                                \n     | Primary Use | LLM↔Tools | Agent Messaging | Task Delegation | Decentralized Coordination | Agent Marketplaces |                                                               \n                                                                                                                                                                                     \n     Key Insight: These protocols are complementary, not competitive. MCP handles tool integration, ACP/ACP handle agent-to-agent communication, SBP provides decentralized          \n     coordination without direct messaging, and ANP enables open-internet discovery.                                                                                                 \n                                                                                                                                                                                     \n     For IDAHO-VAULT, you'd likely want ACP for agent communication and SBP for the swarm coordination layer. MCP would handle tool integration, and ANP could enable discovery      \n     across different vault instances.                                                                                                                                               \n                                         