---|---------------|------------|----------------|\n+| **Control Flow** | Linear (query → response) | Cyclical (plan → act → observe → adapt) | Parallel + Decentralized |\n+| **Autonomy** | None (stateless) | Partial (maintains context) | Full (self-directing) |\n+| **Specialization** | General-purpose | Task-specific | Role-specialized |\n+| **Coordination** | N/A | Sequential/Hierarchical | Decentralized/Self-organizing |\n+| **Scalability** | Limited by model context | Limited by workflow complexity | Linear with agent count |\n+| **Robustness** | Single point of failure | Partial redundancy | Fault-tolerant |\n+\n+### Key Traits of Swarm Agents\n+\n+1. **Persistent Identity**\n+   - Maintains context, role, and purpose across interactions\n+   - Learns from past experiences and patterns\n+\n+2. **Initiative**\n+   - Proactively identifies needs and acts autonomously\n+   - Adapts to changing conditions without external prompts\n+\n+3. **Specialization**\n+   - Domain-specific expertise (coding, testing, research, etc.)\n+   - Collaborates with complementary agents\n+\n+4. **Memory**\n+   - Short-term context for task continuity\n+   - Long-term learning for improvement\n+\n+### Components of a Swarm Agent\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────┐\n+│           SWARM AGENT             │\n+├─────────────────────────────────┤\n+│  📡 Sensor:                       │\n+│     - Perceives environment      │\n+│     - Text, images, data inputs  │\n… omitted 620 diff line(s) across 1 additional file(s)/section(s)\n ─  ⚕ Hermes  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── \n                                                                                                                                                                                     \n     Done! I've created a comprehensive document on AI Agentic Swarming at:                    